WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.550
Two patients lie in the same
hospital, both close to death.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.800
The first is kept alive
by a breathing machine.

3
00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.670
One day, a doctor switches it off.

4
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.000
The second asks for a lethal
injection, and a doctor gives it.

5
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.000
Both patients die.

6
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:22.150
So is switching off a machine morally
different from giving a lethal injection?

7
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.150
Or is a death simply a death?

8
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.620
In this mission, you'll test
the answer of natural law,

9
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:31.000
the theory that comes from Aquinas.

10
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:35.090
Then you'll build an argument map, and
weigh up a claim on which thoughtful people

11
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.370
disagree.

12
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.230
Your mission: weigh up whether switching
off a machine and giving a lethal injection

13
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.190
really differ.
